            <ArticleTitle>Unusual hemodynamic response during exercise-induced angina pectoris.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>365-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with coronary artery disease exhibited reduction in systemic arterial pressure and striking changes in pulmonary artery wedge pressure and pulse contour during an episode of exercise-associated angina pectoris. There is suggestive evidence that these phenomena were secondary to marked but reversible exacerbation of mitral regurgitation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
